        <groundspeak:log id="683266960">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP430 High Level Bridge

Found on the way to work this morning. Pulled into the parking area close to the cap location next to a couple of cars. Walked over and quickly found the red flagging.  Cleaned leaves out of the divot below the flagging and easily found the cap. After a bit of cleaning with some leaves the cap numbers were easily read. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Walking back to the car noticed a fellow making a fire in the fireplace near the parking area. Then noticed the other car's windows were steamed up. Looks like he was sleeping in his car here. Seemed to want to be left alone so I just got in my car and left.  The things you run into early in the morning while caching. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="604821673">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.529350" lon="-113.514583" />
          <groundspeak:date>2016-05-28T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP430 - High Level Bridge

Out picking up caches with fuzeebear in the river valley and what pops up on the GPS? Brass cap! Yay! The gps was bouncing me around a fair bit, we went up and down the 'cliff' face, finally getting led to a tree with a bit of flagging tape on it, directly above the cap heh.  This one is in great shape.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
